{title: Buffalo Gals}
{artist: John Hodges, 1844}
{key: G}
{tempo: 110}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, americana}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[G]As I was walking down the street
[D]Down the street, [G]down the street
A pretty little gal I chanced to meet
[D]Oh, she was [G]fair to see

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Buffalo gals, won't you come out tonight
[D]Come out tonight, [G]come out tonight?
Buffalo gals, won't you come out tonight
And [D]dance by the light of the [G]moon
